From: OpenWrt Fix <fix@openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: fix NULL pointer dereference in ieee80211_txq_may_transmit

When txqi->schedule_order is uninitialized or zeroed (next == NULL),
list_empty(&txqi->schedule_order) checks (head->next == head), which evaluates
to false because (0x0 == head) is false. This incorrectly assumes the list is
non-empty and calls list_del_init(&txqi->schedule_order).
list_del_init then attempts next->prev = prev, which dereferences (0x0)->prev (0x8),
triggering a kernel Data Abort / Oops.

Fix this by ensuring txqi->schedule_order.next is non-NULL before checking list_empty.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Fix <fix@openwrt.org>
---
--- a/net/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -4252,7 +4252,7 @@ bool ieee80211_txq_may_transmit(struct i
 	return false;
 out:
-	if (!list_empty(&txqi->schedule_order))
+	if (txqi->schedule_order.next && !list_empty(&txqi->schedule_order))
 		list_del_init(&txqi->schedule_order);
 	spin_unlock_bh(&local->active_txq_lock[ac]);

